.TH "HTMLIMAGEELEMENT.SRC" "3JS" "August 31, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
HTMLImageElement.src \- HTMLImageElement: src property
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]src\f[B]\f[R] property of the \f[CR]HTMLImageElement\f[R]
interface specifies the image to display in the \f[CR]<img>\f[R]
element.
It reflects the \f[CR]<img>\f[R] element\(cqs \f[CR]src\f[R] content
attribute.
.PP
Setting \f[CR]src\f[R] property triggers scheduling of a task to fetch
the specified resource; the element does not need to be inserted into
the active document first.
Unless loading is set to \f[CR]lazy\f[R], the image will be fetched
almost immediately (if lazy loading is specified the request is deferred
until the element is near the viewport: which can\(cqt happen until the
element is inserted).
.SH VALUE
A string.
For more information about the syntax of the \f[CR]src\f[R] attribute,
see the HTML \f[CR]<img>\f[R] reference.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Setting the src attribute
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] img = \f[B]new\f[R] Image();
img.src = \(dqexample.png\(dq;
img.alt = \(dqAn example picture\(dq;
.EE
